        "author": "Saima Asad",
        "date": "2015-04-25",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "inspected": "960×694 browser preview",
        "observed": "Close courtyard-side facade: rose brick/plaster, pale lower trim, central two-tier pointed niche framing a dark door, repeated pointed bays, blue/yellow/turquoise mosaic panels and roof frieze, patterned dark shutters. Tall neighboring urban building is host content. No floral or calligraphic motif copied."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masjid_Wazeer_Khan,_Lahore.jpg",
        "author": "Fassifarooq",
        "date": "2016-11-26",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "inspected": "960×725 browser preview",
        "observed": "Courtyard looking west: octagonal minarets with tall inset panels, upper balcony, open chhatri posts, flared eave and shallow dome/finial; five pale ochre prayer-hall domes, tall central pointed iwan and four lower bays, blue/cream/yellow/rose tile fields and continuous frieze. Red paving, green rectangular pool, small court pavilion at left. City, people, pigeons and temporary fixtures omitted. Photos guide approximate appearance, not current measured finish."
      }
    ]
